            <ArticleTitle>U wave alternans in severe ischaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with unstable angina and known heart failure, and marked U wave alternans on the electrocardiogram is reported. Alternans of the U wave with no change in the QRS complex is extremely rare. The relevant literature is reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
